            <ArticleTitle>Oral surgery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>583-601</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An overview of the various possibilities for oral surgery urgent care to the oral region has been presented. Modern treatment procedures have been described. The recent advances in dental science have become superior to what they were just a few short years ago; however, we must never forget the variabilities of human responses to any of our treatment techniques, and we must not be dogmatic in our approach. We should all be able to diagnose, interpret, and alter any of our treatment techniques as necessary.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
